   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "### Quick-Start Checklist\n",
    "\n",
    "- [ ] Set `SEED` and `BIT_GEN` at the top for reproducibility.\n",
    "- [ ] Use `weighted_choice()` for any discrete / categorical sampling.\n",
    "- [ ] Use `plot_distribution(name)` to quickly visualise any supported distribution.\n",
    "- [ ] Use `simulate_poisson_process()` / `simulate_markov_chain()` for stochastic processes.\n",
    "- [ ] Use `BetaBinomialUpdater` for Bayesian conversion-rate problems.\n",
    "- [ ] Use `monte_carlo_integral()` for numerical integration.\n",
    "- [ ] Use `estimate_polynomial_params()` for MCMC parameter recovery.\n",
    "- [ ] Use `qq_plot()` / `ks_test()` to validate distributional assumptions.\n",
    "\n",
    "> Built on concepts from *Applying Math with Python, 2nd Ed.* (Morley, 2022)."
   ]
